  "post": {
    "caption": "Ambarella stock fell 19.8% on Wednesday after the camera-chip maker forecast next-quarter sales of $70M to $75M, down from $115.2M and about 35% below Wall Street's estimate.\nCEO Fermi Wang blamed \"the unprecedented rise in memory prices and the scarcity of memory supply\": customers who can't get memory for their devices are cancelling or delaying chip orders. Bank of America cut its target to $30 from $70.\n\nGet this week's five, free every Saturday → link in bio.\n\n#ambarella #amba #semiconductors #memorychips #chipstocks\n\nSources: StockTitan market close (Nov 25), Stocktwits via Yahoo Finance (Nov 25), Invezz (Nov 25), Blockonomi (Nov 25), GuruFocus via Yahoo Finance (Nov 25; next report date is an estimate). Not investment advice."
